   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription The Anti-Corruption Bureau (ACB) seized ₹2.4 lakh in unaccounted cash from the possession of Hyderabad Metropolitan Water Supply and Sewerage Board (HMWSSB) Joint Director A. According to the ACB, it received an anonymous call alleging that a senior HMWSSB official had collected cash illegally and was carrying it while returning home from office. During the search, ACB officials found ₹2.4 lakh in unaccounted cash in his possession.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后即可解锁 反贪局（ACB）从海得拉巴都市供水与排污委员会（HMWSSB）联合局长A.处查获₹2.4 lakh无法入账的现金。据ACB称，接到匿名举报，称HMWSSB一名高级官员非法收取现金，并在下班回家途中携带现金。搜查期间，ACB人员在他身上发现了₹2.4 lakh无法入账的现金。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription The Anti-Corruption Bureau (ACB) seized ₹2.4 lakh in unaccounted cash from the possession of Hyderabad Metropolitan Water Supply and Sewerage Board (HMWSSB) Joint Director A. Srinivas during a vehicle check on Raj Bhavan Road on Friday (October 24, 2026) night. According to the ACB, it received an anonymous call alleging that a senior HMWSSB official had collected cash illegally and was carrying it while returning home from office. Based on the information, the ACB City Range-II team kept surveillance on the official. At around 7 p.m. on October 24, officials intercepted a Maruti Swift car opposite Metro Residency Apartments on Raj Bhavan Road. The vehicle was found to belong to Mr. Srinivas, who was travelling in it. During the search, ACB officials found ₹2.4 lakh in unaccounted cash in his possession. The ACB said Mr. Srinivas failed to provide a satisfactory explanation for possessing the cash while returning from office and gave inconsistent versions when questioned. The cash was seized under a panchanama for verification of the alleged corruption angle. The ACB said further necessary action would be taken and the Income Tax Department would be informed. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
