   "_dt": 1792916523.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "Hyundai Motor and Kia's combined retail sales in China fell below 10,000 vehicles for the first time this year in September amid sluggish demand, industry data showed Sunday. Hyundai Motor's sales plunged 47 percent on-year to around 4,000 units last month, while Kia's dropped 31 percent to 5,000, according to a Hana Securities report based on China Passenger Car Association (CPCA) data.",
   "summary_zh": "行业数据显示，本周四，现代汽车和起亚在中国的合计零售量9月首次跌破1万辆，原因是需求疲软。据韩亚证券根据中国乘用车协会（CPCA）数据出具的报告，现代汽车上月销量同比下降47%，降至约4,000辆；起亚销量下降31%，降至5,000辆。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Hyundai Motor and Kia's combined retail sales in China fell below 10,000 vehicles for the first time this year in September amid sluggish demand, industry data showed Sunday. Hyundai Motor's sales plunged 47 percent on-year to around 4,000 units last month, while Kia's dropped 31 percent to 5,000, according to a Hana Securities report based on China Passenger Car Association (CPCA) data. Their combined sales fell 39 percent to approximately 9,000 units, with their market share slipping to just 0.6 percent from more than 10 percent in the mid-2010s. The automakers have struggled to revive sales despite introducing electric vehicles (EVs) tailored to the Chinese market. Hyundai's China-specific electric SUV Elexio sold just 251 units in the first nine months of this year, compared with 1,216 in the final three months of last year. The Ioniq V, Hyundai's first China-specific model under its Ioniq brand, sold 558 units in September",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
