   "summary": "Chungnam National University held a town hall meeting on Friday to discuss its future development, including a proposed merger with another national university. The university said the meeting was organized to build consensus on major issues and future development plans, including a proposed merger with Kongju National University.",
   "summary_zh": "忠南国立大学周五举行市民大会，讨论学校的未来发展，包括拟与另一所国立大学合并。该大学表示，此次会议旨在就重大问题和未来发展规划形成共识，其中包括拟与公州国立大学合并。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Chungnam National University held a town hall meeting on Friday to discuss its future development, including a proposed merger with another national university. About 250 people, including faculty members, staff, teaching assistants, students and alumni, attended the meeting at Baekma Hall of the university’s Jeongsimhwa International Cultural Center. The university said the meeting was organized to build consensus on major issues and future development plans, including a proposed merger with Kongju National University. Participants also discussed the Glocal University Project and a support package for flagship national universities, sharing their views on the university’s future. The two-hour meeting began with opening remarks by President Kim Jeong-kyoum, followed by a presentation on the university’s future direction by Kim Young-guk, vice president for external affairs. “The meeting provided a forum for university members to better understand the key issues facing Chungnam National University, discuss its future direction and share their views,” President Kim said. Representatives of various university groups and other attendees then shared their views in an open discussion. The university said the meeting was intended to foster mutual understanding among its members and lay the groundwork for its future growth",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
