   "title": "President Lee mulls picking justice minister nominee from 2 prosecutor-turned-lawmakers",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/politics/20261025/president-lee-mulls-picking-justice-minister-nominee-from-2-prosecutor-turned-lawmakers",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:22:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1792916523.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "President Lee Jae Myung is mulling over selecting a justice minister nominee from between two prosecutor-turned-lawmakers after his previous pick for the post withdrew his candidacy last month over lobbying allegations, a source at the presidential office said Sunday. Rep. Park Kyoon-taek and Rep. Yang Bu-nam of the ruling Democratic Party of Korea (DPK) are the candidates that Lee is reviewing for justice minister, a source at Cheong Wa Dae told Yonhap News Agency.",
   "summary_zh": "总统办公室一名消息人士周日表示，李在明总统正在考虑从两名由检察官转型为议员的候选人中挑选一位司法部长提名人；此前他提名的人选上月因游说指控退出候选。执政的朝鲜民主党（DPK）议员朴权泽和梁富男是李正在评估的司法部长候选人。青瓦台消息人士向韩联社透露了上述情况。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "President Lee Jae Myung is mulling over selecting a justice minister nominee from between two prosecutor-turned-lawmakers after his previous pick for the post withdrew his candidacy last month over lobbying allegations, a source at the presidential office said Sunday. Rep. Park Kyoon-taek and Rep. Yang Bu-nam of the ruling Democratic Party of Korea (DPK) are the candidates that Lee is reviewing for justice minister, a source at Cheong Wa Dae told Yonhap News Agency. \"After a lengthy deliberation, Lee is reviewing the choice between Park and Yang. An official nomination is expected to be made soon,\" the source said. In a Cabinet reshuffle in late August, Lee nominated Rep. Kim Seung-won of the DPK to lead the justice ministry. A parliamentary confirmation hearing was held last month, but Kim withdrew his candidacy amid controversy over various allegations, including lobbying for a COVID-19 treatment drug. Amid a two-month vacancy in the justice minister post, Lee is believed to be carefully reviewing the nomination while considering public sentiment. Park and Yang, both first-term lawmakers in the DPK's stronghold in the southwestern Honam region, formerly served as prosecutors. Park is among a group of DPK lawmakers calling for dropping Lee's criminal indictments, claiming they were brought by politically motivated prosecutors. Yang was appointed a co-chief of the party's legal affairs committee in 2022, when Lee was the head of the DPK, to manage Lee's legal issues",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "af"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
