   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription An Assistant Engineer of the Andhra Pradesh Eastern Power Distribution Company Limited (APEPDCL) was found dead on a road at Kondapeta near Rajam on Sunday (October 25, 2026). Her family has alleged that it was not a road accident. According to the police, she fell near Kondapeta, and her body was found on a stretch of road with little traffic.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后即可解锁这些内容。安得拉邦东部电力分销有限公司（APEPDCL）的一名助理工程师于10月25日星期日在拉贾姆附近的孔达佩塔公路上被发现死亡。她的家人称，这并非交通事故。警方表示，她在孔达佩塔附近跌倒，遗体是在一段车流较少的路段上发现的。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription An Assistant Engineer of the Andhra Pradesh Eastern Power Distribution Company Limited (APEPDCL) was found dead on a road at Kondapeta near Rajam on Sunday (October 25, 2026). Her family has alleged that it was not a road accident. The police identified the deceased as Gunda Lalita Kumari, about 30, a native of Cheepurupalli. She was riding her two-wheeler towards Rajam on Sunday morning. According to the police, she fell near Kondapeta, and her body was found on a stretch of road with little traffic. Her family members said it was not a road accident and asked the police to investigate the incident. The police have registered a case and begun an investigation. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
