   "title": "Usage of terrorism as instrument of statecraft simply unacceptable: Jaishankar",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/usage-of-terrorism-as-instrument-of-statecraft-simply-unacceptable-jaishankar/article71622789.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:20:02 +0530",
   "_dt": 1792914602.0,
   "ageDays": 0.04,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription The usage of terrorism as an \"instrument of statecraft\" is simply unacceptable, and it can never be justified or rationalised, External Affairs Minister S. Jaishankar said on Sunday (October 25, 2026) and flagged that it continues because \"not all states really display zero tolerance\" to the menace. Its usage as an instrument of statecraft is simply unacceptable.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后即可解锁这些内容。外交部长S. 贾伊尚卡尔于10月25日星期日表示，将恐怖主义作为“国策工具”使用“完全不可接受”，绝不可能得到任何合理化解释；他还指出，恐怖主义之所以仍在持续，是因为“并非所有国家都真正对这一威胁表现出零容忍”。将恐怖主义作为国策工具使用完全不可接受。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription The usage of terrorism as an \"instrument of statecraft\" is simply unacceptable, and it can never be justified or rationalised, External Affairs Minister S. Jaishankar said on Sunday (October 25, 2026) and flagged that it continues because \"not all states really display zero tolerance\" to the menace. Despite history holding so many lessons on it, \"some still allow political calculations to take precedence\", he said in his address at an event here without naming any country. At an event held in New Delhi to mark the 75th anniversary of Chinmaya Mission, he underlined the importance of peace, especially amid the ongoing conflicts in the world. \"Let us consider the indivisibility of peace. Now, war anywhere threatens peace everywhere,\" the Union minister said. He cited the conflicts in Ukraine and the West Asia region currently underway, and asserted that India expresses global sentiment when it says that dialogue and diplomacy is the only solution. \"Terrorism is another deadly threat to peace. Its usage as an instrument of statecraft is simply unacceptable. It can never be justified. It can never be rationalised. Yet, it continues because not all states really display zero tolerance. Despite history, holding so many lessons, some still allow political calculations to take precedence,\" Mr. Jaishankar said. The world must, therefore, develop sharper awareness about this common threat, and it must come together with stronger resolve and counter terrorism in all its forms and manifestations, he said. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
