   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Connectivity between Visakhapatnam and the national capital received a boost with Akasa Air launching a daily direct flight service between Delhi and ASR International Airport at Bhogapuram on Saturday (October 24, 2026). Akasa Air is the third airline to operate direct flights on the route.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁这些内容。随着Akasa Air于2026年10月24日星期六开通德里与位于Bhogapuram的ASR国际机场之间的每日直飞航线，Visakhapatnam与印度首都之间的交通连接得到提升。Akasa Air是第三家在该航线上运营直飞航班的航空公司。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Connectivity between Visakhapatnam and the national capital received a boost with Akasa Air launching a daily direct flight service between Delhi and ASR International Airport at Bhogapuram on Saturday (October 24, 2026). The service marks the airline’s return to the city. Akasa Air is the third airline to operate direct flights on the route. The service is expected to cater to growing demand for air travel driven by business, government-related travel, education, tourism and visits to friends and relatives. It will also offer passengers greater seating capacity, schedule flexibility and competitive fares. “The launch of Akasa Air’s daily direct service to Delhi marks an important milestone in strengthening connectivity between Visakhapatnam and the national capital,” said Kanwarbir Singh Kalra, CEO of GVIAL. The service is operated with Boeing 737 MAX 8 aircraft. Flight QP 1842 departs Delhi at 5.55 a.m. and arrives at Visakhapatnam at 8.20 a.m. Flight QP 1843 departs Visakhapatnam at 9.05 a.m. and arrives in Delhi at 11.30 a.m. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
