   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription A 12-year-old boy who went to his tuition by walk has been missing in Krishnagiri district since Friday evening (October 23, 2026). Sanjay, a resident of Indian Bank Street at Singarapettai near Uthangarai in Krishnagiri district, is a Class VII student at a private school in Uthangarai.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后即可解锁 一名12岁男孩自周五傍晚（2026年10月23日）起在克里希纳吉里县失踪。桑贾伊是克里希纳吉里县乌坦加赖附近Singarapettai的Indian Bank Street居民，就读于乌坦加赖一所私立学校的七年级。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription A 12-year-old boy who went to his tuition by walk has been missing in Krishnagiri district since Friday evening (October 23, 2026). According to the police, T. Sanjay, a resident of Indian Bank Street at Singarapettai near Uthangarai in Krishnagiri district, is a Class VII student at a private school in Uthangarai. On Friday, he went to school and returned to home in the evening. Around 5 p.m., he went to his tuition centre at Periya Kadai Street in Singarapettai by walk. However, he did not return home and when his parents inquired with the tuition centre, they found that he did not reach the tuition. Shocked by this, his parents started searching for him in various locations and, around 9 p.m., they lodged a complaint with the Singarapettai police. The police registered a case, verified the CCTV footage in the locality, and found the boy asking for a lift and getting on a two-wheeler with a person. The police are on the lookout for the two-wheeler to identify if he was kidnapped. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
