   "published": "Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:12:37 +0530",
   "_dt": 1792914157.0,
   "ageDays": 0.05,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription The 12-year-old boy who had gone missing in Krishnagiri district was rescued by the Pulianthope police in Chennai on Saturday (October 24, 2026) night. A senior official of the Greater Chennai Police said Sanjay, son of Thirunavukkarasu was reported missing on Friday (October 23) with his father registering a boy missing complaint at the Singarapettai police station of Krishnagiri district.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁这些内容。那名在克里希纳吉里县失踪的12岁男孩于星期六（2026年10月24日）夜间被金奈的普里安托普警方救出。大金奈警察局的一名高级官员表示，蒂鲁纳武卡鲁萨之子桑贾伊于星期五（10月23日）被报告失踪，其父亲在克里希纳吉里县辛加拉佩泰警察局提交了男孩失踪报案。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription The 12-year-old boy who had gone missing in Krishnagiri district was rescued by the Pulianthope police in Chennai on Saturday (October 24, 2026) night. A senior official of the Greater Chennai Police said Sanjay, son of Thirunavukkarasu was reported missing on Friday (October 23) with his father registering a boy missing complaint at the Singarapettai police station of Krishnagiri district. However, on Saturday evening, the boy who was standing alone outside the Perambur railway station asked an auto driver to take him to the Dr. MGR Central railway station. The auto driver who became suspicious, questioned the boy who informed him about running away from home. The auto driver then alerted the Pulianthope police station. Following instructions from the police, the auto driver brought the boy to the Pulianthope police station. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
