   "summary": "Joseph Vijay on Sunday (October 25, 2026) condoled the death of popular Chef K. Dhamodharan who was widely known as ‘Chef Dhamu’. In a post on X, Mr. Vijay said, through his culinary skills and distinctive approach, Dhamodharan brought the art of cooking closer to the people through television programmes.",
   "summary_zh": "约瑟夫·维贾伊星期日（2026年10月25日）对广受喜爱的厨师K·达莫达兰之死表示哀悼。达莫达兰广为人知的名字是“Dhamu厨师”。维贾伊先生在一篇X帖子中表示，达莫达兰凭借其烹饪技艺和独特方法，通过电视节目让烹饪艺术更贴近民众。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Tamil Nadu Chief Minister C. Joseph Vijay on Sunday (October 25, 2026) condoled the death of popular Chef K. Dhamodharan who was widely known as ‘Chef Dhamu’. In a post on X, Mr. Vijay said, through his culinary skills and distinctive approach, Dhamodharan brought the art of cooking closer to the people through television programmes. In 2010, he set a Guinness World Record for the longest cooking marathon by an individual. He was also honoured with the Padma Shri and his demise is a great loss to the culinary world, Mr. Vijay added. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
