   "title": "Govt extends duty-free raw sugar import window till Dec 31 to ease festive supplies",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/business/Industry/govt-extends-duty-free-raw-sugar-import-window-till-dec-31-to-ease-festive-supplies/article71615656.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:25:47 +0530",
   "_dt": 1792752947.0,
   "ageDays": 1.91,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription The Government has extended the duty-free import deadline for 1 million tonnes of raw sugar under the Tariff Rate Quota (TRQ) to December 31 to boost domestic supplies during the festive season. According to a finance ministry notification, the import window has been extended to December 31, 2026. The extension is aimed at securing supplies whenever international prices ease enough to make imports viable.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁全文。尼日利亚政府将关税配额（TRQ）下100万吨原糖的免关税进口期限延长至12月31日，以在节日季增加国内供应。财政部通知称，进口窗口已延长至2026年12月31日。此次延长期限旨在把握国际价格降至足以使进口具备经济可行性时的供应机会。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription The Government has extended the duty-free import deadline for 1 million tonnes of raw sugar under the Tariff Rate Quota (TRQ) to December 31 to boost domestic supplies during the festive season. According to a finance ministry notification, the import window has been extended to December 31, 2026. On August 20, the government allowed imports of 1 million tonnes of raw sugar until October 31. So far, around 2.6 lakh tonnes has been imported, according to industry data. Industry sources said imports have remained subdued due to a lack of price parity. The extension is aimed at securing supplies whenever international prices ease enough to make imports viable. Besides allowing imports, the Government has taken a series of measures like imposing stockholding limits on traders to ensure adequate domestic supplies and keep prices in check amid tight availability. Sugar production for the 2025-26 marketing year (October-September) is now estimated at 306 lakh tonnes, down from an earlier forecast of 343 lakh tonnes. Annual domestic demand is pegged at 280-285 lakh tonnes. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "af"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "eco",
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
