   "title": "When Mali, Burkina Faso and Niger left ECOWAS last year, many of us felt the ripple in markets and border posts.",
   "url": "https://x.com/thecindyyy_/status/2113608881159254415",
   "snippet": "When Mali, Burkina Faso and Niger left ECOWAS last year, many of us felt the ripple in markets and border posts. Last week in Dakar the two sides sat down properly and agreed to build a practical cooperation framework — not a return to membership, but rules that could ease trade, movement and security cooperation.\nOrdinary people have been paying the price of the split in higher costs and delays. If these working groups deliver clear, fair rules, that is what actually matters on the ground. The question is whether we keep the focus on livelihoods or let process swallow the purpose.\nThis is Society & Diplomacy. Where Global Issues Meet Everyday Life.\n#SocietyAndDiplomacy \n#HalimaAbdullah",
   "body": "When Mali, Burkina Faso and Niger left ECOWAS last year, many of us felt the ripple in markets and border posts. Last week in Dakar the two sides sat down properly and agreed to build a practical cooperation framework — not a return to membership, but rules that could ease trade, movement and security cooperation.\nOrdinary people have been paying the price of the split in higher costs and delays. If these working groups deliver clear, fair rules, that is what actually matters on the ground. The question is whether we keep the focus on livelihoods or let process swallow the purpose.\nThis is Society & Diplomacy. Where Global Issues Meet Everyday Life.\n#SocietyAndDiplomacy \n#HalimaAbdullah",
