   "title": "How a Village Self-Defence Group Turned Into Nigeria’s New Cross-Border Terror Bridge In 2017, border villages in Sokoto invited an armed he",
   "url": "https://x.com/ADEYUSUF_ia/status/2113399368250167644",
   "snippet": "How a Village Self-Defence Group Turned Into Nigeria’s New Cross-Border Terror Bridge\n\nIn 2017, border villages in Sokoto invited an armed herding militia, Lakurawa to shield them from bandits.\n\nBy 2026, that former vigilante force had evolved into one of Nigeria’s fastest-spreading terror threats:\n• Taxed Kebbi and Sokoto communities ₦50m ($36,000) in March 2026 just to let clerics preach Ramadan tafsir\n• Killed 162 civilians in Woro and Nuku, Kwara State after villages rejected its rule\n• Built an active corridor linking Sahelian jihadists (ISGS/JNIM) toward northern Benin and central Nigeria\n\nHistory’s hardest internal security lesson repeats: when the state leaves a vacuum, outsourced community defence rarely stays defensive for long.",
